<BlogPost title="DeepSeek Harness Model Setup — Official API, OpenCode Go &amp; Free Agnes | dshbase" description="Three ways to power DeepSeek Harness: the official DeepSeek API, the OpenCode Go token plan (60 credits for $5), and Agnes free unlimited API. Setup steps and base URLs." currentPath="/blog/dsh-model-setup/" category="Guide">
  <h1>DeepSeek Harness <span class="accent">model setup</span></h1>
  <p class="muted small" style="margin-bottom:20px">August 14, 2026 · dshbase</p>

  <p>DeepSeek Harness is model-agnostic — point it at any OpenAI-compatible API. Here are the three setups the community actually uses, from the official API to free tiers.</p>

  <h2>1. Official DeepSeek API</h2>
  <p>The default and simplest. Register at <a href="https://platform.deepseek.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">platform.deepseek.com</a>, create an API key, and set it in dsh:</p>
  <pre class="code-block"><code>DEEPSEEK_API_KEY: sk-your-key-here
# base URL: https://api.deepseek.com</code></pre>
  <p>Store it in <code>~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml</code> or under <strong>Settings → Models</strong>. No referral program — just direct registration and pay-as-you-go.</p>

  <h2>2. OpenCode Go — $5 for $60 of credits</h2>
  <p><a href="https://opencode.ai/go?ref=S7Y0RD7RBS" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenCode Go</a> is a token plan: <strong>first month $5 gives you $60 of credits</strong>, billed per model. The most useful models on it are DeepSeek and MiMo. It pairs cleanly with dsh — hand dsh a task, let OpenCode's model credits do the work.</p>
  <pre class="code-block"><code># add OpenCode Go as a custom provider in dsh
# base URL + your OpenCode Go key + model (deepseek / mimo)</code></pre>
  <p>Get it here (referral): <a href="https://opencode.ai/go?ref=S7Y0RD7RBS" target="_blank" rel="noopener">opencode.ai/go?ref=S7Y0RD7RBS</a></p>

  <h2>3. Agnes — free, unlimited multimodal API</h2>
  <p>Agnes (by Sapiens AI) offers a <strong>permanently free</strong> multimodal API — the <code>agnes-2.5-flash</code> coding model is free with no rate limit, covering code, image, and more. A domestic China endpoint is also available.</p>
  <pre class="code-block"><code># add Agnes as a custom OpenAI-compatible provider in dsh
# base URL (agnes endpoint) + your Agnes key + model: agnes-2.5-flash</code></pre>
  <p>Register on the Agnes platform, then add it as a custom provider in dsh's Settings → Models (lowercase Provider ID + base URL + key + model).</p>

  <h2>How to add a custom provider in dsh</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>Open <strong>Settings → Models</strong> in the web UI.</li>
    <li>Add a provider: lowercase ID, base URL, protocol, your key, and at least one model.</li>
    <li>Use <strong>Get available models</strong> to verify the endpoint.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Full model configuration is in the <a href={tutorialUrl}>tutorial</a>.</p>

  <h2>Which to pick?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Official DeepSeek</strong> — simplest, pay-as-you-go.</li>
    <li><strong>OpenCode Go</strong> — best bang for buck early on ($60 credits for $5).</li>
    <li><strong>Agnes</strong> — totally free, great for testing or light use.</li>
  </ul>
</BlogPost>
